    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Per-user: last 24h vs own baseline",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "description": "Each user's last 24h against their own prior-7d daily average (offset 24h, so the tested window is excluded from what it is compared against). Sorted ascending, so a collapse sits at the top.\n\nNear-0% with a non-zero 24h figure means their client still connects and authenticates before being torn down — a block. A flat 0 with nothing at all is more likely someone who stopped using it. Bytes are the only per-user metric xray exposes, so that read is a judgement, not a measurement.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 40
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (user) (increase(xray_user_downlink_bytes_total{job=\"xray_user_stats\"}[24h]))",
          "instant": true,
          "format": "table",
          "editorMode": "code"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
